e-write premium 0.000232625 with premium 0.0028950950000000003 reserved 0.0171024\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a billing difference in the stored July responses. They report cache-write tokens, and OpenAI prices those above ordinary input. The ledger currently settles both at the ordinary rate. I’ve checked the archived July 10 Data Center call against the published rates."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The July send is **not ready**. The latch and sequence handling are fixed. The budget ledger still releases money that the provider’s published rates say was spent.\n\n## Blocking finding\n\n**Luna cache writes are billed above the rate the ledger uses.** On the stored July 10 Data Center call, OpenAI reported 9,305 cache-write tokens. `llm_cost` settles that call at $0.002662. At the published default cache-write rate, the same usage costs $0.002895. I found positive cache-write counts in all 1,620 stored judge responses. The July 10 call still fits its reservation, but settlement releases the difference back into the shared budget. That breaks the cap argument even if every individual call costs less than its reservation. This finding comes from stored usage and published pricing. The round-10 fake established only how the ledger reacts to an overrun. [Settlement code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:240) · [Luna pricing](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-luna#pricing) · [OpenAI cache-write accounting](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/prompt-caching)\n\n**The output bound is sound. The input bound still needs a source.** OpenAI documents that `max_completion_tokens` includes reasoning. The byte argument bounds tokens for the text presented to a byte-level tokenizer. It leaves the provider’s message framing, hidden content, and schema processing to be bounded separately. I found no provider guarantee that those fit `2 × wire bytes + 4,096` on this Chat Completions path. For Jev, TypeSafe publishes a default 64K per-request limit and the input rate. Use that limit for the reserved retry bundle, and keep the upper-bound charge for any attempt whose usage is unavailable. The final response reports usage for its own evaluation. [Reservation code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:227) · [OpenAI completion limit](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/chat/subresources/completions/methods/create#max_completion_tokens) · [TypeSafe model limits](https://docs.typesafe.ai/models#context-length) · [TypeSafe usage fields](https://docs.typesafe.ai/api/system-one#response-usage)\n\n**Before sending:** settle Luna at the applicable rates, including cache writes, and reserve against documented bounds on billable input and output. Re-run the $0 budget check with the stored cache-write response and a retry whose usage is unavailable. If a documented Luna input bound cannot be established, the choice for Alex is whether to wait for a hard cap or authorize the July test with a $0.15 reservation stop and the possibility of a higher bill. I recommend keeping the hard cap. [D694](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10439)\n\n## Verified and nonblocking\n\n- **Latch and send loop.** Both scopes hold one lock through the inner transport. I reran `latch_race` and only A reached that transport. A provider retry runs inside the admitted call while the lock is held. A sequence-level refusal leaves the other sequences eligible to run, and a shared-ledger stop ends the comparison. [Latch](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:56) · [Race check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:286) · [Send loop](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:527)\n- The rollback test now checks the writer’s savepoint before calling its own rollback. For the race test, a barrier at B’s lock acquisition would make the waiting assertion independent of thread scheduling. [Rollback test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_links.py:278) · [Race assertion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:305)\n\n**NOT READY**"}}
